            <div xml:id="d125">

                <pb facs="0278" n="146" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg146"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 EW/7–545: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 125 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Political Adviser in
                        Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Murphy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-05T11:00:00-04:00">July 5, 1945—11
                            a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>61. I wish to invite you to be present at the forthcoming meeting of the three
                    Heads of Government.</p>
                <p>Following is the list of State Department personnel totalling thirty-six people
                    who make up my party: Secretary Byrnes; Ambassador Harriman, Ambassador Murphy;
                    Assistant Secretary Clayton, Assistant Secretary Dunn; Ben Cohen, Donald Russell
                    and Walter Brown, Special Assistants to the Secretary; H. F. Matthews, C. E.
                    Bohlen, Llewellyn Thompson, Edward Page, Emilio Collado, James Riddleberger,
                    Emile Despres, Cavendish Cannon, George Allen, J. C. Vincent, Eugene Dooman,
                    Philip Mosely, Charles Yost, Colonel John Wise, R. B. Reams, Wilder Foote and an
                    administrative and secretarial staff of twelve.</p>
                <p>I should appreciate it if you would take proper steps to make sure that
                    appropriate arrangements are made in Berlin for this group which is scheduled to
                    arrive July 13.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                        <lb/> J[oseph] C. G[rew] </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
